"""Overlay completed fix evidence while preserving the original audit snapshot."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
review=p.parent/'review-2026-10-30'
summary=json.loads((p/'validation-summary.json').read_text())
resolutions=json.loads((p/'resolutions.json').read_text())
findings=json.loads((review/'findings.before-fixes.json').read_text())
e=html.escape
s=(review/'report.before-fixes.html').read_text()
s=s.replace('Nestimate code review — 30 October 2026','Nestimate code review and fixes — 30 October 2026')
s=s.replace('Nestimate: extensive code review','Nestimate: extensive code review and fixes')
s=s.replace('Source version 1.0.1 · HEAD dcdd7135','Source version 1.0.1 · Fixes in working tree above dcdd7135')
s=re.sub(r'<p class="lead">.*?</p>', '<p class="lead">All 12 reproduced defects have been corrected and regression-tested. The separate case-drop reliability concern is also resolved with an explicit target option. The original audit evidence is preserved below, followed by the current implementation status.</p>',s,count=1)
s=s.replace('This was a review and report task. No package implementation, exported API, documentation source, or production tests were changed. Evidence scripts intentionally demonstrate the current defects; they are not tests of repaired behavior.', 'The user subsequently authorized fixing every finding. Production code and help topics have been updated, with four dedicated regression files, release notes, the missing reference-index entries, and a three-platform package-check workflow. No commit or push was made. <a href="report.before-fixes.html">The original review</a> remains available unchanged.')
s=s.replace('<h2>Prioritized findings</h2>','<h2>Original findings and completed resolutions</h2><p>All observed-behavior and source-location descriptions in the finding cards refer to the pre-fix review snapshot. Each card now starts with its implemented correction and regression test.</p>')
for f in findings:
 r=resolutions[f['id']]
 f.update(resolution_status='fixed',resolution=r['resolution'],regression_test=r['regression_test'])
 marker=f'<section class="card" id="{f["id"]}">'
 replacement=marker+f'<p><strong>Resolved.</strong> {e(r["resolution"])} Regression coverage: <code>tests/testthat/{e(r["regression_test"])}</code>.</p>'
 s=s.replace(marker,replacement)
s=s.replace('<strong>Observed behavior.</strong>','<strong>Before fix.</strong>')
s=s.replace('<strong>Why it happens.</strong>','<strong>Original cause.</strong>')
s=s.replace('<strong>Recommended correction / workaround.</strong>','<strong>Original review recommendation.</strong>')
s=s.replace('<h2>Separate design concern: reliability of existing edges versus the whole graph</h2>', '<h2>Resolved: reliability of existing edges versus the whole graph</h2><p><strong>Implemented:</strong> <code>casedrop_reliability(target = "auto")</code> uses existing edges for unscaled/unthresholded transition methods and all cells for association or transformed networks. Explicit <code>"existing"</code> and <code>"all"</code> select either target; the resolved target is stored in each result. The original reproducer now agrees with the whole-graph maximum deviation. Coverage: test-fix-review-higherorder.R. The next paragraphs describe the original limitation.</p>')
s=s.replace('The current help explicitly describes present-edge-only metrics','At review time the help explicitly described present-edge-only metrics')
s=s.replace('Decide whether the API should offer an explicit existing-edge/whole-graph target, or restrict the structural-zero rationale to methods for which it holds. A user assessing whole-network reliability should not infer that newly appearing edges have been included.', 'The new target option and method-aware default now make this distinction explicit.')
validation=f'''<table><tr><th>Final check</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td>Complete development suite outside sandbox</td><td>{summary['passed']:,} passed; {summary['failed']} failed assertions; {summary['error']} errors; {summary['warning']} warnings; {summary['skipped']} skips. {summary['files']} files. This is one complete final run, not a combination of partial reruns.</td></tr><tr><td>New regression assertions</td><td>{summary['new_passed']} passing assertions across four dedicated files. Numerical/structural oracles cover every finding and the case-drop target change.</td></tr><tr><td>Source build with vignettes</td><td>Successful. The final archive includes the code, documentation, tests and release notes.</td></tr><tr><td>R CMD check --as-cran --no-manual</td><td>{e(summary['package_check'])}. final-check.log and final-00check.log retained. PDF manual was not built.</td></tr><tr><td>htna 0.3.1 reverse dependency</td><td>{e(summary['htna_check'])}. Checked against fixed Nestimate in an isolated temporary library.</td></tr><tr><td>Visual preview</td><td><a href="../fixes-2026-10-30/landscape-preview.html">Rendered landscape preview</a> covers weighted/concatenated fits and tied-value surfaces. Preview was presented for the repository-required visual review; automated plotting checks pass. {e(summary.get('visual_review','No visual approval is claimed.'))}</td></tr></table><p>Development warnings are retained in the log; they include deprecation, zero-variance, sign and misfit diagnostics. The full suite was run outside the sandbox because lavaan CPU detection fails in the sandbox. No dependency was upgraded. The local runtime remains R 4.5.2/macOS with idiographic 0.4.0.9004 and cograph 2.7.11; minimum-version and remote-platform compatibility are not established by this run.</p><p><a href="../fixes-2026-10-30/final-full-tests.csv">Final test results</a> · <a href="../fixes-2026-10-30/resolutions.json">Resolution manifest</a> · <a href="../fixes-2026-10-30/final-check.log">Package-check log</a> · <a href="../fixes-2026-10-30/revdep-htna-final.log">Reverse-dependency log</a>.</p>'''
s=re.sub(r'<div id="validation">.*?</div>','<div id="validation">'+validation+'</div>',s,flags=re.S)
a=s.index('<h2>Compatibility and release readiness</h2>');b=s.index('<h2>Evidence and reproducibility</h2>')
s=s[:a]+'''<h2>Compatibility and release readiness</h2><p>The documented 1.0.1 migration notes for plot_mosaic, sequence_plot argument positions and hypergraph_centrality defaults remain in effect. These fixes add explicit behavior: stars-only literal state labels are reserved by the pattern syntax and now raise nestimate_bad_input; older saved custom-weight composite fits need rebuilding to retain their weighting specification; and landscape inputs must represent their stored sequence chain. The new case-drop auto target includes potentially emerging association edges.</p><p>All five previously omitted pkgdown topics have been added to the reference index. A push/PR workflow now configures the full development suite and package checks on Linux, macOS and Windows. The workflow was parsed locally but has not been run on GitHub. No full pkgdown site rebuild, minimum-dependency matrix, PDF manual build or release deployment is claimed.</p><p>Before release, inspect CI on the supported platforms and check minimum dependency versions. The current work addresses all reported defects; these broader release checks remain environment validation rather than unresolved findings.</p>'''+s[b:]
s=s.replace('Run scripts from the package root, for example', 'Original reproduction scripts are retained as historical evidence and intentionally assert pre-fix behavior; some should now fail. Run new regression tests with <code>devtools::test(filter = "fix-review")</code>. The original command example was')
s=s.replace('The scripts load current development source with pkgload. Some intentionally caught errors and warnings are the evidence being demonstrated. Reproductions validate current observed behavior; they must be rewritten to assert repaired behavior when fixing code.', 'The new tests assert repaired behavior and include public-API, invariance and analytic controls. Final results and the resolution manifest are stored in audit_folder/fixes-2026-10-30/.')
s=s.replace('This report describes the reviewed source snapshot. No fixes have been applied as part of this review.', 'Updated after the user-authorized fixes. Original counterexamples and review history remain preserved; final validation describes the modified working tree.')
(review/'report.html').write_text(s)
(review/'findings.json').write_text(json.dumps(findings,indent=2))
print('Updated report and all 12 structured resolutions.')
